# No dashes or hyphens in website copy

Never use em dashes (—), en dashes (–), or hyphens (-) in user-facing text: UI strings, headings, metadata, FAQs, cancel guides, blog posts, or marketing copy.

## Use instead

| Avoid | Use |
|-------|-----|
| Em dash (—) | Period, comma, colon, or middle dot (·) |
| En dash (–) | "to" for ranges |
| Hyphenated compounds (One-time, money-back, 2-3) | Spaces or rephrase ("One time", "money back", "2 to 3") |

## Allowed (not copy)

CSS class names, URLs, code identifiers, file names, and third party brand names that contain hyphens (e.g. Disney+ domains).

## Examples

- Bad: `100% Private — Everything stays on your device`
- Good: `100% Private. Everything stays on your device`

- Bad: `Drop your last 2-3 months of statements`
- Good: `Drop your last 2 to 3 months of statements`

- Bad: `One-time payment — no monthly fee`
- Good: `One time payment. No monthly fee`
